MT6797 BSP AutoK import
======================

Source: X20-96-board, commit de3e0196cc3799775052af899c90f9a105e07492,
kernel-3.18/drivers/mmc/host/mediatek/mt6797/.

autok.c is the complete BSP source. The only edit rejects a fifth boundary
before the original parser writes past bd_info[4]. The original rejection
after that write was too late. No valid scan, filter, edge, delay, cycle,
latch, repeat count, platform constant or fallback rule has been changed.
There is no added window-selection algorithm or card-specific parameter.

autok.h and sync_write.h are byte-identical to the BSP. msdc_reg.h changes
only the include path of sync_write.h. tune-path.h contains the verbatim
msdc_init_tune_path() from msdc_tune.c. mt_sd.h supplies the small host view
needed by AutoK and copies the original bit-field/MMIO helpers verbatim.

The outer mtk-sd-mt6797-autok.c adapter supplies the removed timeval API for
elapsed-time logging, declarations required by the modern compiler, and
the mainline host layout. The tuning sender still polls the controller
directly, including its resets, FIFO handling, interrupt status, and latch
test. It is not replaced with mmc_send_tuning(). The adapter sets/restores
PIO mode for that sender and propagates failures to the modern MMC core.

mtk-sd.c routes removable MT6797 SDR104 through this implementation. Modern
MMC core retune requests rerun the original BSP re-AutoK operation; clock
changes reapply the saved BSP parameter array. A power-off discards that
card's result. PAD_TUNE1 is preserved across runtime PM, like the BSP timing
save/restore. eMMC tuning is unchanged. Imported offline/eMMC entry points
are not called by this integration.

Run x20-sbc/tools/test-mt6797-bsp-autok-import.py from the X20 workspace to
check the entire imported source against the BSP and the declared edits.
The original BSP fallthrough in autok_pad_dly_sel() is deliberately retained;
modern GCC reports -Wimplicit-fallthrough there.

Building and matching sources do not prove SD stability. See the workspace
docs/bsp/20261018-alignment/bsp-autok-* evidence for actual acceptance.
